# .gitignore
#
# Written by Claude (Anthropic model, Claude Opus 4.5) at the direction of
# Edwin West, for the SecretPrinter project.
#
# Session handoffs added by Claude (Anthropic model, Claude Opus 5) at the
# direction of Edwin West, 2026-09-14.
#
# Kept short on purpose. A sprawling ignore file copied from a template makes it
# hard to notice when something that SHOULD be committed is being silently
# excluded. Every rule below is here because this repository actually produces
# the thing it names.

# ---- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/

# ---- Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code user state -----------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# ---- Test and coverage output -----------------------------------------------
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
*.opencover.xml

# ---- NuGet ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
packages/
.nuget/

# ---- OS noise ---------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---- Local configuration and secrets ----------------------------------------
# A configuration file describes one machine: its adapter names, its printer,
# and the UUID that installation advertises. None of that is secret - the UUID
# is broadcast in the clear on the local network - but none of it belongs to
# anybody else either.
#
# The UUID matters for a second reason. If one were committed as an example,
# every copy of this repository would advertise the same identity, and two
# SecretPrinters on one network claiming one UUID is exactly what REQ-ADV-005
# exists to prevent. Configurations are produced by:
#
#   SecretPrinter.Service.exe --print-example-config
#
# which is documented in docs/operating.md, along with generating a fresh UUID.
secretprinter.json
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json
*.local.json
local.settings.json

# Signing material must never be committed. Release signing uses Azure Trusted
# Signing (REQ-DIST-004), which does not require a certificate file in the repo;
# these patterns exist so an accidental local certificate cannot be added.
*.pfx
*.snk
*.p12
*.key

# ---- Diagnostic captures ----------------------------------------------------
# Output from tools/SecretPrinter.Listen can contain device names from the
# operator's own network. Captures are ignored by default so they are published
# deliberately, after review, rather than by accident.
captures/
*.mdns-capture.txt

# ---- Session handoffs -------------------------------------------------------
# Working notes written at the end of one session and read at the start of the
# next. They are kept outside the repository for two reasons.
#
# They describe the operator's own network - machine names, both subnets, the
# printer's address, and hardware identifiers including MAC addresses. That is
# the same category of detail the pre-publication audit redacted from test data
# (docs/findings/2026-09-04-pre-publication-audit.md), and it does not become
# safe to publish by arriving in a different file.
#
# And they are deliberately speculative: they carry hypotheses, half-tested
# theories, and next steps that may not survive contact with the next
# measurement. docs/findings/ is curated and is meant to be trustworthy on
# sight. Mixing the two would cost the findings that property.
#
# Anything in a handoff that turns out to matter belongs in a finding or in the
# README, where it is subject to the same standards as everything else here.
secretprinter-handoff-*.md
